---
import {
  breadcrumbSchema,
  faqSchema,
  JsonLd,
  profilePageSchema,
} from "~/components/json-ld";
import { EMAIL, SITE_URL } from "~/config/site";
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/base-layout.astro";

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: "Who is Leonardo Maldonado?",
    answer:
      "A senior full-stack engineer based in Valencia, Spain, originally from Franca, Brazil. He has 8+ years of experience, all of it remote, mostly in TypeScript. He was the only frontend engineer on Spaceship's domain search at Namecheap, which sold more than 3 million domains, and he created 33 JavaScript Concepts (66K GitHub stars).",
  },
  {
    question: "What is he building right now?",
    answer:
      "SetLuca, a DM sales platform for experts, creators and coaches. It reads incoming DMs on Instagram, Messenger and Telegram, scores each lead and replies in the creator's own voice. It's TypeScript end to end: Hono on Cloudflare Workers, Inngest, TanStack Start, PostgreSQL and Drizzle. On the side he builds Strait, an open-source engine for background jobs and workflows on Postgres.",
  },
  {
    question: "What did he build at Namecheap?",
    answer:
      "From November 2021 to June 2026 he was a senior front end engineer and the only frontend engineer on Spaceship's domain search. He built it from scratch in React and TypeScript, including a WebSocket pricing engine for 500+ TLDs, bulk search for up to 100 domains and pricing in 30+ currencies. The product sold more than 3 million domains.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is 33 JavaScript Concepts?",
    answer:
      "An open-source guide to core JavaScript concepts, from closures and prototypes to async patterns. Leonardo published it in 2018. It has 66K GitHub stars, community translations in 40+ languages, and GitHub named it one of the top open-source projects of 2018.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is his stack?",
    answer:
      "Mostly TypeScript, front and back: React, Next.js, TanStack Start, Node.js, Hono, Cloudflare Workers, PostgreSQL and Drizzle. He writes Go for Strait.",
  },
  {
    question: "Where is he based?",
    answer:
      "Valencia, Spain (CET). He speaks Portuguese natively, works in English and has some Spanish.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is he open to new work?",
    answer:
      "Yes. He's open to senior full-stack and freelance roles, remote or partly on-site in Europe.",
  },
  {
    question: "How can I contact him?",
    answer: `Email ${EMAIL}, or find him as leonardomso on GitHub, LinkedIn and X.`,
  },
];

const breadcrumbs = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: "Home", url: SITE_URL },
  { name: "About", url: `${SITE_URL}/about` },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · Leonardo Maldonado"
  description="Leonardo Maldonado is a software engineer in Valencia, Spain. He was the only frontend engineer on Spaceship's domain search at Namecheap, created 33 JavaScript Concepts and is building SetLuca."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/about`}
>
  <JsonLd data={profilePageSchema} />
  <JsonLd data={breadcrumbs} />
  <JsonLd data={faqSchema(faqItems)} />

  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

  <div class="stack text">
    <p>I grew up in Franca, Brazil, and now live in Valencia, Spain.</p>

    <p>I’ve been writing software professionally since 2019, all of it remote. For four and a half years I was the only frontend engineer on <a href="https://www.spaceship.com/domain-search/">Spaceship’s domain search</a> at <a href="https://www.namecheap.com">Namecheap</a>. I built it from scratch and owned everything from architecture to releases: real-time pricing over WebSockets for 500+ TLDs, bulk search, and pricing in 30+ currencies. It sold more than 3 million domains while I was there.</p>

    <p>Now I’m building <a href="https://setluca.com">SetLuca</a>, a DM sales platform for experts, creators and coaches. It reads incoming DMs on Instagram, Messenger and Telegram, scores each lead and replies in the creator’s own voice. It’s TypeScript end to end: Hono on Cloudflare Workers, Inngest, TanStack Start, PostgreSQL and Drizzle.</p>

    <p>On the side I build <a href="https://strait.dev">Strait</a>, background jobs and multi-step workflows that run on the Postgres database you already have, with no Redis or separate queue. It’s a single Go binary, open source under Apache-2.0.</p>


    <p>In 2018 I published <a href="https://github.com/leonardomso/33-js-concepts">33 JavaScript Concepts</a> as a study guide for myself. It now has 66K stars and translations in 40+ languages, and <a href="https://github.blog/2018-12-13-new-open-source-projects/#top-projects-of-2018">GitHub named it one of the top projects of 2018</a>. I still maintain it.</p>

    <p>I’ve also written 100+ articles on React, TypeScript and frontend performance for <a href="https://blog.logrocket.com/author/leonardomaldonado/">LogRocket</a> and <a href="https://www.telerik.com/blogs/author/leonardo-maldonado">Progress</a>. I like explaining things clearly and helping other developers learn.</p>

    <p>I mostly work in TypeScript, front and back, and I like owning a product from the first architecture decision to every release.</p>

    <p>Outside of work I walk around Valencia, read, and start side projects that sometimes ship. I speak Portuguese and English, and some Spanish.</p>

    <p>I’m open to senior full-stack and freelance roles, remote or partly on-site in Europe. If you want to talk, <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>email me</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-faq">
    <h2 id="h-faq">Questions</h2>
    <div>
      {faqItems.map((item) => (
        <details class="disclosure">
          <summary>{item.question}</summary>
          <p>{item.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
